@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] mila-session-hegel-properties
Hegel properties MUST cover the private `refusal_code` closed set against an
independent byte-class oracle with totality on arbitrary bytes; the private
`validate_ssh_keys` envelope, count and per-key field lattice, including its
`Bounds` and `Refused` outcomes; `decode_listing` authority projection,
malformed identity and authority refusal, duplicate ids, cursor preservation,
and canonical row order independent of the server's order; and the command
grammar bounds of `machine_create`, `machine_resize`, `device_register` and
`thread_action`, observed through a fake Porsche endpoint that records each
exec line and its stdin: accepted inputs send exactly one grammar-checked line
with the expected command, arguments and options (and the push key only on
stdin), and refused inputs send nothing. Pagination, refresh atomicity,
sharing and machine reads stay with the scripted real-TCP russh tests; the
fake endpoint does not verify Porsche's own authorization.
